{"title":"Litespeed Launches Four New Titanium eBikes for Road and Gravel","link":"https://bikerumor.com/litespeed-launches-four-new-titanium-ebikes-for-road-and-gravel/","date":1793374074000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-hero-Large.jpeg\" width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" alt=\"(Photos / Litespeed)\" /></p>\n<p>Today things get a bit electrified and amplified as Litespeed debuts four new bicycles you may never have expected. Meet Litespeed’s new lineup of titanium road and gravel E-bikes: the Sustain and Harmonizer for the road, and the Overdrive and Distortion for gravel.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes lean Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-lean-Large-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photos / Litespeed)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>These new eBikes are still hand-built in the same Tennessee factory that has produced other Litespeed frames. And they’re designed to bring the high-performance and legendary ride of Litespeed titanium to a larger cycling audience.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes modes Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-modes-Large-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Look, you and I both know that Litespeed has spent pretty much its whole existence making light and refined titanium frames. Now the brand is putting that dedication into electric bikes, hoping that road and gravel riders who usually side-eye a motor might be ready to reconsider.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes grav grav Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-grav-grav-Large-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>The Motor</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The new lineup uses the Mahle X20 System, a lightweight assist setup designed for performance bikes. Litespeed says it delivers 275 watts of peak power and assistance up to 20 mph from a 250 Wh battery, with Eco, Sport, and Boost modes. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"818\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes duo Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large-297x190.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large-120x77.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-duo-Large-768x491.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>It’s a Class 1 system, so the motor only helps while you’re pedaling, and Litespeed claims the pedal feel stays natural. The motor sits in the rear hub, which is where HED enters the picture: each bike gets a HED hand-built road or gravel wheelset laced to the Mahle hub, with a choice of carbon or high-performance alloy rims.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"978\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes cornering Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large-297x227.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large-120x92.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large-768x587.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cornering-Large-1178x900.jpeg 1178w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes comin' in hot Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-comin-in-hot-Large-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>What About the Frame?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The frames use new custom-formed Superform eSL6/4 and Pure eLW titanium tubesets. Litespeed says these tubes produce the lightest titanium E-bike frames possible. Buyers can pick from a wide range of high-end components, specs, and sizes, just like any other Litespeed.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"704\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes cool shot Large\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large-297x163.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large-120x66.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-cool-shot-Large-768x422.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>CEO Chris Pascarella admits he was a skeptic. “<em>I had bought into the stigma that riding an E-bike was a sign of surrender,” he said. He’s since changed his tune, arguing the bikes let you keep up with a fitter partner, enjoy that dream Col, or “commute to work without risk of hitting Zone 2.</em>”</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Motor &amp; Battery Specs</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Motor</strong>: MAHLE X20 rear hub</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Power</strong>: 250 W</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Torque</strong>: 65 Nm</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Battery</strong>: 250 Wh</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Extender</strong>: Optional eX1 available</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Class</strong>: Class 1, assists up to 20 mph</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>System</strong>: 3.2 kg (7.05 lbs), including battery</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>OK, let’s check out the bikes!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://litespeed.com/collections/sustain\" target=\"_blank\">Sustain</a> eRoad Racing Bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $12,599 </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes sustain feture hero\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-feture-hero-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>“<em>The Sustain is built on Litespeed’s racing pedigree. With signature Superform tube shaping and the innovative sheet-formed Superform eSL6/4 titanium top tube, it delivers incredible stiffness and sets the bar for low weight and high-speed performance. Complete with Shimano Ultegra Di2 groupset and HED V45 carbon wheelset.</em>“</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes sustain motor\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-motor-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes sustain front derr\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-sustain-front-derr-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Frame Specs</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Frame Material: Superform eSL 6/4 Titanium Tubeset (3AL/2.5V + 6AL/4V Top Tube)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Seatpost Diameter: 31.6mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Derailleur Hanger: UDH</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Derailleur Mount: 34.9mm Clamp-on</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cable Routing: Fully-Integrated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Spacing: 12 x 100 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Axle Spec: M12 x 1.5, 120- 125 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Spacing: 12 x 142 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Axle Spec: M12 x 1.0, 164- 167 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (2x – Shimano): 54/40t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>MaxChainring Size (2x – SRAM): 56/43t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chainring Size (1x): 46t Max</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rotor Size: Max 160mm front and rear</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tire size: 700x35mm max</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://litespeed.com/collections/harmonizer\" target=\"_blank\">Harmonizer</a> eRoad Bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $9,999</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes harmonizer feature hero\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-harmonizer-feature-hero-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>“<em>The Harmonizer is built using Litespeed’s Pure eLW titanium tubeset, carefully shaped and constructed to deliver a smooth and comfortable ride, mile after mile. With 35mm of tire clearance paired with relaxed endurance geometry, the legendary Litespeed titanium ride just got better. Harmonizer starts at $9,995 outfitted with a Shimano 105 Di2 drivetrain and HED V45 carbon wheelset.</em>“</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube.jpeg\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-top-tube-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes motor\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-motor-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Frame Specs</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Frame Material: Pure eLW 3AL/2.5V Titanium Tubeset</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Seatpost Diameter: 31.6mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Derailleur Hanger: UDH</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Derailleur Mount: 34.9mm Clamp-on</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cable Routing: Fully-Integrated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Spacing: 12 x 100 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Axle Spec: M12 x 1.5, 120- 125 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Spacing: 12 x 142 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Axle Spec: M12 x 1.0, 164- 167 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fork Offset: 47mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rigid Fork Length: 381mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (2x – Shimano): 54/40t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>MaxChainring Size (2x – SRAM): 56/43t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chainring Size (1x): 46t Max</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rotor Size: Max 160mm front and rear</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tire size: 700x35mm max</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://litespeed.com/collections/overdrive\" target=\"_blank\">Overdrive</a> eGravel Race Bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $12,599</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"910\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes overdrive feature hero\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero-297x211.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero-120x85.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero-768x546.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-overdrive-feature-hero-1266x900.jpeg 1266w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>“<em>Litespeed’s flagship gravel E-bike is built with race-inspired geometry, 50mm of tire clearance, and features Litespeed’s proprietary lightweight sheet-formed Superform eSL6/4 top tube. It comes complete with Shimano GRX 1X Di2 827 components and a HED Lancaster<br />carbon wheelset. The Overdrive delivers the direct feel and high-speed handling that has become synonymous with Litespeed race bikes.”</em></p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes left\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-left-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes right\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Frame Specs</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Frame Material: Superform eSL 6/4 Titanium Tubeset (3AL/2.5V + 6AL/4V Top Tube)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Seatpost Diameter: 31.6mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Derailleur Hanger: UDH</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Derailleur Mount: 34.9mm Clamp-on</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cable Routing: Fully-Integrated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Spacing: 12 x 100 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Axle Spec: M12 x 1.5, 120- 125 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Spacing: 12 x 142 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Axle Spec: M12 x 1.0, 164- 167 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fork Offset: 50mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rigid Fork Length: 420mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (2X): 48/31t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (1X): 46t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chainring Size (1x): 46t Max</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rotor Size: Max 180mm front and 160mm rear</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tire size: 700x50mm max</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://litespeed.com/collections/distortion\" target=\"_blank\">Distortion</a> eGravel Bike</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $9,999</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"926\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes distortion feature hero\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero-297x215.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero-120x87.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero-768x556.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-distortion-feature-hero-1244x900.jpeg 1244w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>“<em>The Distortion is Litespeed’s all-rounder gravel rig, delivering classic lines and ride feel with Litespeed’s Pure eLW 3AL/2.5V titanium tubeset. 54mm of tire clearance and adventure-ready geometry give riders the confidence needed to tackle bigger rides and rougher roads. Outfitted with SRAM’s Rival AXS XPLR groupset and HED Lancaster carbon wheels</em>.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes right top tube\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-right-top-tube-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"853\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear.jpeg\" alt=\"Litespeed Titanium eBikes rear\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Litespeed-Titanium-eBikes-rear-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Frame Specs</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Frame Material: Pure eLW 3AL/2.5V Titanium Tubeset</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Seatpost Diameter: 31.6mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Derailleur Hanger: UDH</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Derailleur Mount: 34.9mm Clamp-on</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cable Routing: Fully-Integrated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Spacing: 12 x 100 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Front Axle Spec: M12 x 1.5, 120- 125 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Spacing: 12 x 142 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rear Axle Spec: M12 x 1.0, 164- 167 mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fork Offset: 50mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rigid Fork Length: 420mm</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (2X): 48/31t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Max Chainring Size (1X): 42t</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chainring Size (1x): 46t Max</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rotor Size: Max 180mm front and 160mm rear</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tire size: 700x54mm max</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Litespeed combines titanium and a quiet, light assist system. It seems like a smart pairing. Add the hand-built HED wheelset, and this could be one of the more interesting premium E-road and gravel options on the market currently. Hit the link below for more details. </p>\n\n\n\n<p><em><a href=\"https://litespeed.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Litespeed.com</a></em></p>","author":"Ron Frazelle","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/litespeed-launches-four-new-titanium-ebikes-for-road-and-gravel/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"f422260fd22e90d61a15d05931501b5d8e9d3b0baffe834f3b947133c0f90e95","category":"Cycling"}